    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 19th with a top-heavy lineup led by **Yordan Alvarez** (76.88) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.81), both of whom offer the highest efficiency potential against their respective right-handed matchups. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a cornerstone play, leveraging his elite xwOBA against Bibee, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our primary engine for the scarcest category; his dynamic platoon advantage against Gausman, combined with a high likelihood of a stolen base attempt against a pitcher with a slower delivery, makes him an essential start. **Junior Caminero** (69.42) rounds out our elite tier, benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against Poulin, where his power profile aligns perfectly with the favorable SP_xERA of 5.00.\n\nThe most critical roster decision centered on **Christian Yelich** (58.43), who narrowly missed the \"Strong\" tier. While his leadoff spot and moderate SP_xERA provide stability, his dynamic platoon disadvantage against the left-handed P\u00e9rez, M forced him into a marginal utility role. Consequently, we are prioritizing the superior platoon splits of **Lars Nootbaar** (63.94) in the outfield, as his matchup against Lugo, S offers a more favorable SP_xERA floor. Conversely, **Colt Keith** (40.66) and **Casey Schmitt** (41.80) are hovering near the floor of our starting threshold; they remain in the lineup solely to protect our daily game caps, as no deeper bench assets\u2014with **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** off today\u2014are available to improve upon their projected production. While our minor league depth including **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds** remains unavailable, we will monitor the lineup card for **Dillon Dingler**, whose scoring is bolstered by a favorable left-handed platoon draw against Eisert.",
